Chapter: QuotesUntrusted

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  quotes "sha256:71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b" as Sorted
  trusting "fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff" "30a23f41fc17ec2aac012d0755750484a535afbcff80882094d569bbc7bdefff" 1000
  trusting above 5000

 The work is present, it hashes to the digest it was quoted by, it is
 signed, and the signature verifies. Everything the bytes can prove
 about themselves, they prove.

 The key that signed it scores one thousand, and this chapter said it
 would take nothing below five. A signature says who stands behind a
 definition; it does not say we have to take their word for it. That
 is the fourth guard, and it is the only one that is a judgement rather
 than a fact.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("sorted=" & show (sort-ascending 5))
  end

